And who carried the team?

269
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:35,840
Also me.

270
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,840
Good grief, how could it be anything
less than perfect?

271
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:42,400
I think I look a bit stiff.

272
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:44,640
It feels like I'm lacking any emotion.

273
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,040
You might be missing some emotion,

274
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:47,480
but I'd hate...

275
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:49,800
to miss you.

276
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:52,920
Seriously?

277
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,200
I can't handle this.

278
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,760
- How do I handle this much love?
- Look it up.

279
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:57,560
Hold on.

280
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:01,440
- "How to handle a lovey-dovey couple?"
- I wanna know it, too.

281
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:03,840
Soh...

282
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:05,800
You're Soh, right?

283
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:09,800
P'Ten?

284
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:12,360
Whoa, finally getting to meet you.

285
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:13,960
I thought your voice was cute enough,

286
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:15,520
but you're even cuter in person.

287
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,240
Can I touch your cheeks?

288
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,920
You're the total opposite of this guy.

289
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,600
He's not even cute in person.

290
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:29,600
Ten.

291
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,520
What's up,

292
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:32,360
dear friend?

293
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:35,920
How do you know Soh?

294
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:39,440
James wanted me to play the game
with him the other day,

295
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,240
and P'Ten was playing, too.

296
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,760
You're already acting tough, I see.

297
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,920
I was just stopping by to say hi.

298
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:50,440
Stay away from my boy.

299
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:55,120
You're still as hot-headed as ever.

300
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:59,360
Watch out, or your team might not
be able to handle your sh*t.

301
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:03,160
If you ever can't take it anymore
and want to switch teams,

302
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,360
let me know, Soh.

303
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,560
With your skills,

304
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:10,800
staying in a bottom-tier team like this,

305
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,120
to be honest,

306
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:14,240
is a total waste of talent.

307
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,120
B.S. Brothers, you're done.
Blue Viper, get ready.

308
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,800
Take them to the set.

309
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,600
I'm actually quite surprised

310
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,280
that your team lucked its way
into the playoffs.

311
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:31,760
But don't get ahead of yourself.

312
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:34,360
Forget about beating my team.

313
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,840
Just survive the lower bracket first.

314
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:38,560
Then you can worry about
facing my team.

315
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:13,200
Come out and talk to me.

316
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:20,040
Why did you say such sh*tty things?

317
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:22,320
Why?

318
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,160
Was I supposed to be nice to him?

319
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,360
That's not it.

320
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:29,840
Can't you just talk to him normally
like you do to me?

321
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:31,200
Do you seriously not know

322
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,120
who started this?

323
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:35,080
Even if he started it,

324
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:36,960
you didn't have to give him
the time of day.

325
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:38,720
What's the point

326
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,760
of talking sh*t to him like that?

327
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:46,640
So I'm the one in the wrong again?

328
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:52,840
You're always taking his side.

329
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:55,840
Ten...

330
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:21,080
My face hurts so damn much.

331
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:25,200
I never imagined
I'd have to smile this much in my life.

332
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,600
For real.

333
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:31,360
I want to soak in an onsen
until my bones literally melt.

334
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,280
Listen up.

335
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:34,800
You all did a great job.

336
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:37,080
Go get some rest now, okay?

337
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,360
Pack your things and get out.

338
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:40,320
Listen.

339
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,520
(Daily Training Schedule)
Let's discuss the new training schedule.

340
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:44,280
What?

341
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,520
Right now?

342
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:50,040
We only have two weeks left to prepare.

343
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:52,040
So, starting from tomorrow,

344
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:54,160
we'll be practicing
14 hours a day, no days off.

345
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:55,080
What?

346
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,040
No days off?

347
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:01,560
Is this a gaming camp
or a military boot camp?

348
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:03,320
Exactly.

349
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:06,560
If it's that intense,
we're gonna be toast.

350
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:07,280
Hey,

351
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,880
other teams train even harder.

352
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:10,520
Just look at Blue Viper.

353
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:12,480
If we want to stay ahead of them,

354
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:13,920
we've got to out-train them.

355
00:22:15,680 --> 00:22:17,320
Before you go overhauling the plan,

356
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,760
did you even ask the team leader?

357
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:23,280
I'm not on board with this.

358
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,360
Wait, what?

359
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:28,120
Look, training more
is definitely a good thing,

360
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:30,840
but overtraining can wreck your bodies.

361
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:33,280
You'd be hurting the team
without even realizing it.

362
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,600
I understand both sides.

363
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:51,360
How about this?

364
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:56,160
Let's try increasing
the practice time just a little bit.

365
00:22:56,360 --> 00:22:58,120
Maybe one extra hour a day.

366
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:01,800
And on days off,
we could just practice in the morning.

367
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,960
How does that sound?

368
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:06,840
Good!

369
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:10,400
I'll draft up a new schedule, then.

370
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:13,000
Now, go home and get some rest.

371
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:14,920
Get out of my cafe.

372
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,120
Why?

373
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:56,440
Why does our team
keep messing up the timing right here?

374
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,200
Focus, Three.

375
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:02,720
Focus! Focus, Three!

376
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:21,520
Oh, Soh?

377
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:23,360
What are you doing here?

378
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:26,920
Well, I called you,

379
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,640
but you didn't pick up.

380
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:30,880
I was worried,
so I came to check on you.

381
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:32,760
I'm sorry.

382
00:24:32,800 --> 00:24:35,920
I must've left my phone charging
on the bed, so I didn't hear it.

383
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:37,880
Come in first.

384
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:52,240
Whoa, are you seriously
drinking this much caffeine?

385
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:56,560
Why?

386
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,240
Worried about my heart racing?

387
00:24:59,320 --> 00:25:01,600
Let me tell you,
even a hundred cups of coffee

388
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:04,120
can't make my heart race
as fast as being with you, Derpy Kid.

389
00:25:05,040 --> 00:25:06,720
Before your heart races because of me,

390
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:09,400
you'd better worry about
a caffeine-induced heart failure.

391
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:17,480
And why is your room so dark?

392
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:18,920
Is the lightbulb broken?

393
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:25,000
Whoa, and the screen is so bright, too.

394
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:30,960
Well, I don't think it is.

395
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:43,360
P'Three...

396
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:47,120
Yes?

397
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,440
Do you have any blue light glasses?

398
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:56,880
You need to take care of your eyes.

399
00:25:57,640 --> 00:26:00,320
Because if your eyes get so bad
you have to wear glasses,

400
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,880
you might lose your cool look.

401
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:05,880
I don't mind losing my look,

402
00:26:08,360 --> 00:26:11,480
but if I couldn't see your face anymore,
that's what I can't stand.

403
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:15,560
Come on.

404
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:17,040
You're still joking around.

405
00:26:17,040 --> 00:26:18,560
I'm seriously worried about you.

406
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:19,920
Oh, come on.

407
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,240
Do you know why?

408
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:24,240
Because I love the way you look
when you're worried about me.

409
00:26:24,320 --> 00:26:25,840
It's just so adorable.

410
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:28,360
P'Three.

411
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:32,680
But I don't like it
when you don't take care of yourself.

412
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:37,840
I understand...

413
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:40,680
that you want to lead the team
to the championship.

414
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:45,000
But if anything happens to you,

415
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:47,080
our team will lose its backbone.

416
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:51,600
I get it now.

417
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:54,760
Then...

418
00:26:55,840 --> 00:26:57,560
can I move into your room?

419
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:01,080
My room?

420
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:05,000
Yeah. I'll be crashing at your place
until the tournament ends.

421
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:08,120
And we can have our own private practice

422
00:27:08,480 --> 00:27:09,600
and special training sessions.

423
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,680
Just the two of us.

424
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:15,520
Special training sessions?

425
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:16,640
That's right.

426
00:27:17,520 --> 00:27:18,200
Special?

427
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:20,160
- Yeah, special training sessions.
- Special...

428
00:27:22,720 --> 00:27:23,800
I mean...

429
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:26,120
we can sync up our timing
for Jungle and Support.

430
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:27,160
Sound good?

431
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:33,920
Oh, right. Sounds good.

432
00:27:34,480 --> 00:27:35,400
Right?

433
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:38,840
Now's your chance.
If you want to keep me in line,

434
00:27:38,960 --> 00:27:39,840
you can.

435
00:27:39,840 --> 00:27:42,000
Or if you want to take away my coffee,

436
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:43,840
make me wear my glasses,

437
00:27:44,480 --> 00:27:48,480
or just sit beside me
and nag until my ears go numb,

438
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:49,720
you can do that, too.

439
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:51,120
Good, right?

440
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:55,440
Okay. Sure. Deal.

441
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:56,800
It's great, isn't it? I get it.

442
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,240
Let me pack my stuff real quick.
Be right back.

443
00:27:58,600 --> 00:27:59,280
P'Three!

444
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,400
I haven't agreed to anything yet.

445
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:14,560
Are you moving in
temporarily or permanently?

446
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:15,760
Can I stay permanently?

447
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:20,400
Thanks, Soh.

448
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:23,600
Let's just put these away
and get some rest.

449
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:25,200
I've watched all your replays.

450
00:28:25,280 --> 00:28:26,800
There are tons of things
you need to fix.

451
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:29,200
You'd better be ready.

452
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:32,840
It's gonna be
an intense practice tomorrow.

453
00:28:42,880 --> 00:28:45,440
Are you a centipede or something?
Why do you own this many shoes?

454
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:49,160
To be a champion,
you have to always be prepared.

455
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:51,440
This pair is for Monday practice,

456
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:53,920
and this one
is my lucky color for Tuesday.

457
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:55,080
These are the real deal.

458
00:28:55,080 --> 00:28:57,920
I'll wear them for the opening match
to bring us luck,

459
00:28:57,960 --> 00:29:01,040
and I'll also wear them
when I go up to claim the trophy.

460
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:04,680
You're really serious about this.

461
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:05,400
Of course.

462
00:29:05,520 --> 00:29:07,360
Don't you have any running shoes?

463
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:09,760
I wanted to ask you to go for a run.

464
00:29:11,880 --> 00:29:15,000
Yeah, that sounds like a good idea,
taking the team to exercise.

465
00:29:15,040 --> 00:29:16,360
That's not what I meant.

466
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:17,800
I mean...

467
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:22,920
Running through my mind
so that I'll love you all day.

468
00:29:30,400 --> 00:29:31,360
Very good.

469
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:33,560
You know how to use wordplay now?

470
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:34,600
That's awesome.

471
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:35,960
You've totally leveled up.

472
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,960
- Look.
- Whoa!

473
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,560
That's so cool.

474
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:43,080
You have so much stuff on your desk.

475
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:44,600
If you want to watch your replays,

476
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:47,600
you can watch them on this screen.
It's crystal clear.

477
00:29:48,920 --> 00:29:50,880
Even if there are hundreds of things
on your desk,

478
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,560
there's only you in my heart.

479
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:01,880
Uh...

480
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:08,080
I just wanted to cheer you up,

481
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:10,080
but it seems I'm making it worse.

482
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:12,240
Wait, what?

483
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,600
I was just impressed
by how hard you were trying.

484
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:17,920
How did you even come up
with all these lines?

485
00:30:21,120 --> 00:30:22,200
- Good. Now...
- I...

486
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:23,920
I think that was pretty impressive.

487
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:26,720
Do you think I should grow a beard?

488
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:29,600
Well, it would look cool,

489
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:31,960
- but I think it's better if you don't.
- Why's that?

490
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:34,880
The fans actually voted
that it'd give me a daddy vibe.

491
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:37,360
But your biggest fan is right here,

492
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:40,240
and he has unanimously voted...

493
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:41,840
against the beard.

494
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:44,000
You're so manipulative.

495
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:44,920
Fine.

496
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:47,280
Give me one good reason

497
00:30:47,600 --> 00:30:49,160
to convince me not to grow it.

498
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:52,600
If you don't,
when you kiss my cheek,

499
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:54,960
- this won't prick me.
- The mustache?

500
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:57,080
If it pricks me, it'll hurt.

501
00:30:58,840 --> 00:30:59,440
Alright.

502
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,760
As you wish.

503
00:31:00,880 --> 00:31:02,800
Only because I care about your cheeks.

504
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,080
I won't grow it, then.

505
00:31:04,120 --> 00:31:06,160
I don't care about
that daddy vibe anymore.

506
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:08,880
P'Three.

507
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:12,120
- You'd better listen to me,
- Whoa...

508
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:14,640
- or you'll get it.
- Get what?

509
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:15,480
I'll get what?

510
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:17,040
- This?
- Ow, P'Three!

511
00:31:17,080 --> 00:31:20,080
Ouch! I told you it hurts. No!

512
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:32,480
Ever since Soh got a boyfriend,
we never see him anymore.

513
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:37,840
When you're in love,
you'd wanna be with the person you love.

514
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:39,680
Jeez.

515
00:31:40,280 --> 00:31:42,640
Check this out, Arm.
Everyone is in love these days.

516
00:31:42,720 --> 00:31:44,680
My feed is full of people
showing off their partners.

517
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,480
When am I going to have
a moment like that?

518
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:56,960
I've made up my mind.

519
00:31:57,120 --> 00:32:00,000
I'm not going
to this tournament all lonely.

520
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:03,320
I'm going to find a partner
to sit and cheer with me.

521
00:32:04,360 --> 00:32:06,640
You've got me here.
Are you still lonely?

522
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:07,920
Come on.

523
00:32:07,920 --> 00:32:09,960
It's a different kind
of relationship, man.

524
00:32:18,080 --> 00:32:20,400
If you can't find anyone,
don't come crawling back to me later.

525
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:21,480
Wait...

526
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:22,800
What's wrong?

527
00:32:24,480 --> 00:32:25,360
Arm!

528
00:32:38,880 --> 00:32:40,240
How is Ten doing, son?

529
00:32:40,320 --> 00:32:43,320
Invite him over for dinner sometime.

530
00:32:44,040 --> 00:32:45,240
I don't know, Mom.

531
00:32:45,800 --> 00:32:47,080
He's probably busy lately.

532
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:48,680
We haven't really talked.

533
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:52,640
Did you two have another fight?

534
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:56,800
No, we didn't fight.

535
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:00,720
I think...

536
00:33:01,200 --> 00:33:03,920
Ten just has a sharp tongue. That's all.

537
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:07,200
He never says what he really means.

538
00:33:08,280 --> 00:33:09,360
Back when you were in school,

539
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:12,040
whenever he had a problem,

540
00:33:12,080 --> 00:33:14,440
he never went to anyone but you.

541
00:33:16,080 --> 00:33:17,120
I think...

542
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:19,880
he probably just wants
his best friend, like you,

543
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:21,960
to just listen to him.

544
00:34:43,720 --> 00:34:46,760
(Soh, are you still up? I have something
I want to talk about.)

545
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:06,120
Hello?

546
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:10,440
(Hello, Soh. I have something
I need to talk to you about.)

547
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:12,960
What is it you want to talk about?

548
00:35:14,080 --> 00:35:17,320
(Well, Blue Viper wants to schedule
a scrim with B.S. Brothers.)

549
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:19,080
Uh...

550
00:35:19,600 --> 00:35:22,520
Why are you asking me about this?

551
00:35:23,320 --> 00:35:26,720
(I thought it'd be easier
to talk to you than to Three.)

552
00:35:28,760 --> 00:35:30,960
A scrim so close to the tournament?

553
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:32,120
Does that mean...

554
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:35,200
Blue Viper will know
all of B.S. Brothers' strategies?

555
00:35:35,960 --> 00:35:39,680
(But your team
will get to know ours, too.)

556
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:45,440
(I just want you to try
talking to your team about it.)

557
00:35:50,080 --> 00:35:52,120
(You can give me your answer tomorrow.)

558
00:36:06,800 --> 00:36:09,640
Yeah! Let's go!

559
00:36:09,720 --> 00:36:11,640
- Want to end it?
- Let's wrap it up.

560
00:36:11,640 --> 00:36:13,320
- Dive in! Go, go!
- Final tower! Let's go!

561
00:36:13,560 --> 00:36:14,720
And then...

562
00:36:14,720 --> 00:36:15,640
And then...

563
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:16,760
And then...

564
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:20,480
How about that, *ssholes?

565
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:23,400
- Get a taste of my god-tier Mage plays!
- That was insane!

566
00:36:23,440 --> 00:36:26,000
You know it.

567
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:29,720
Is something wrong, Soh?

568
00:36:38,760 --> 00:36:40,520
P'Ten called me last night.

569
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:42,840
What?

570
00:36:43,120 --> 00:36:46,600
And he said Blue Viper
wants to scrim with us.

571
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:47,280
Hey.

572
00:36:47,600 --> 00:36:49,720
Is he up to something again?

573
00:36:50,160 --> 00:36:51,640
Don't just go along with his game.

574
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:52,800
Exactly.

575
00:36:53,280 --> 00:36:54,800
If we scrim with them now,

576
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:57,280
it's like we're laying all our cards out
on the table for them.

577
00:36:57,280 --> 00:36:59,280
- Like showing them everything.
- Yeah, right in their faces.

578
00:36:59,320 --> 00:37:00,560
- No way.
- Absolutely not.

579
00:37:03,240 --> 00:37:04,240
I think we should say yes.

580
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:06,400
Hey, are you crazy, Jack?

581
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:08,520
I just said not to play along with them.

582
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,240
The tournament is almost here.

583
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:12,360
Who said we'd show them
our actual strategies?

584
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:14,920
We don't have to play
the way we've been practicing.

585
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:17,240
Just show them
some new, dummy strategies.

586
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:20,120
Now, listen.

587
00:37:21,160 --> 00:37:23,400
Since Blue Viper changed their lineup,

588
00:37:23,440 --> 00:37:25,000
their playstyle has changed, too.

589
00:37:25,080 --> 00:37:28,240
They probably just want to test
their new strategies against us.

590
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:32,160
I agree, P'Toobtub.

591
00:37:33,280 --> 00:37:34,840
It's fine if we lose, I guess.

592
00:37:35,160 --> 00:37:37,720
At least we can gather
some intel on them

593
00:37:37,720 --> 00:37:40,240
so that we can counter them
on match day.

594
00:37:45,160 --> 00:37:46,280
Let's do it.

595
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:48,520
Let's dig up everything we can!

596
00:37:48,520 --> 00:37:50,320
Losing doesn't matter. It's a scrim!

597
00:37:50,320 --> 00:37:51,720
Did you say losing doesn't matter?

598
00:38:13,720 --> 00:38:15,520
Let's just do our best, P'Three.

599
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:18,440
And no matter what the outcome is,

600
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:21,240
we will be right here
fighting alongside you.

601
00:38:55,120 --> 00:38:56,240
We, B.S. Brothers, are ready.

602
00:38:56,680 --> 00:38:58,240
Are you ready, Blue Viper?

603
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:08,480
We're ready.

604
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:10,760
If you're ready, let's start the match.

605
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:14,720
(Welcome to Arena of Valor.)

606
00:39:24,880 --> 00:39:26,480
Gank him! I can see him.

607
00:39:26,560 --> 00:39:28,280
Look who's here. Get him!

608
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:30,160
- Let's do it.
- Let's do it.

609
00:39:35,840 --> 00:39:37,240
Three, fall back. Don't engage yet.

610
00:39:37,760 --> 00:39:39,880
Chill out. Don't get tilted, man.

611
00:39:42,160 --> 00:39:44,360
- Three's roaming solo.
- Nice.

612
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:45,120
Let's go!

613
00:39:58,280 --> 00:40:00,160
- My boy, Three.
- What a noob.

614
00:40:19,400 --> 00:40:21,560
- Get him! Dive in!
- You asked for it.

615
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:24,120
- Oh, splitting up?
- Go.

616
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:31,440
- Get him! Go, go!
- Dive in, dive in!

617
00:40:43,800 --> 00:40:45,960
P'Three, we're down on gold. Calm down.

618
00:40:45,960 --> 00:40:47,320
Just farm your items first.

619
00:40:47,520 --> 00:40:48,680
Wait until you have your gear to fight.

620
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:50,360
Pathetic.

621
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:52,520
- My boy, Three.
- Noob.

622
00:41:02,160 --> 00:41:05,000
- He's just an idiot.
- Steamroll them. Keep going.

623
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:06,400
In three...

624
00:41:06,560 --> 00:41:09,680
- Get him!
- Aw, aren't you gonna protect the tower?

625
00:41:09,880 --> 00:41:12,280
- Why didn't you follow up?
- You need to watch your teammates.

626
00:41:16,760 --> 00:41:17,880
You got me killed, too.

627
00:41:18,520 --> 00:41:19,840
Hey, get over here!

628
00:41:20,040 --> 00:41:21,240
Wait for me.

629
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:30,320
What the hell are you guys doing?

630
00:41:31,320 --> 00:41:32,600
Come on, reset.

631
00:41:36,920 --> 00:41:38,800
He keeps going off on his own.
His teammates are probably losing it.

632
00:41:38,800 --> 00:41:40,600
How did he even make it to the league?

633
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:43,600
Get him. Let's make him cry.

634
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:44,920
His team's carrying him so hard.

635
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,720
Hey, go for it!

636
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:52,880
Ten is leading in gold.
Can you just stay back?

637
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:54,000
Where the hell are you guys?

638
00:41:54,040 --> 00:41:55,640
Look at my HP!
How am I supposed to engage?

639
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:56,960
They're right at the tower. Get them!

640
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:59,280
- You just dove in all by yourself!
- Please stay calm.

641
00:42:03,520 --> 00:42:05,280
Now that's over.

642
00:42:05,560 --> 00:42:06,560
That's it.

643
00:42:08,600 --> 00:42:10,000
See? I told you.

644
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:12,680
When you're the real deal,
it just shows.

645
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:16,240
It's okay, everyone.

646
00:42:16,520 --> 00:42:17,920
It's alright. You all did your best.

647
00:42:18,360 --> 00:42:20,000
How can you say it's okay?

648
00:42:20,640 --> 00:42:22,920
Hey, chill out. It's just a scrim.

649
00:42:22,920 --> 00:42:24,520
But why couldn't we control
the damn game at all?

650
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:26,200
Because you were so obsessed
with chasing down Ten.

651
00:42:26,240 --> 00:42:27,280
You didn't care about a damn thing.

652
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:28,800
How did you expect to control the game?

653
00:42:28,920 --> 00:42:30,000
Sh*t your mouth.

654
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:32,840
Why didn't you follow me?
Read the game for once.

655
00:42:32,880 --> 00:42:35,280
- This is why you keep losing.
- Read the game?

656
00:42:35,280 --> 00:42:38,200
You played like sh*t
and still expected others to follow you?

657
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:39,040
Tell me!

658
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:40,200
That's enough, Three.

659
00:42:40,560 --> 00:42:42,880
You were so blinded
by your need to beat Ten

660
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:45,360
- that you didn't care about us anymore.
- I didn't care about you?

661
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:46,880
I didn't?

662
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:51,160
And all that talk about
B.S. Brothers becoming champions,

663
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:52,840
was it just to look cool?

664
00:42:52,880 --> 00:42:55,800
I'm the one staying up all night,
watching replays,

665
00:42:55,960 --> 00:42:57,960
finding ways to fix our gameplay
every single day,

666
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:00,120
and trying to keep your heads
in the game when you're tilting.

667
00:43:00,240 --> 00:43:03,400
After everything I've done,
you're saying I don't care about you?

668
00:43:09,080 --> 00:43:10,800
(We are B.S. Brothers)

669
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:12,120
I did all of this

670
00:43:12,600 --> 00:43:15,240
because I wanted to see you
become champions, just like you said.

671
00:43:24,160 --> 00:43:25,280
I'm sorry, everyone.

672
00:43:25,280 --> 00:43:27,440
Three and I are heading out for today.

673
00:43:31,520 --> 00:43:32,920
Goddammit!

674
00:43:33,560 --> 00:43:34,480
Take it easy.

675
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:45,320
(We are B.S. Brothers)

676
00:43:59,080 --> 00:44:01,320
(Are you sure you're playing RoV?)

677
00:44:01,360 --> 00:44:03,560
(If you're not gonna watch your team,
just go 1v1.)

678
00:44:03,600 --> 00:44:06,640
(With this score, forget the Pro League.
You'd lose to kindergarteners.)

679
00:44:06,640 --> 00:44:09,480
(They were destroyed
just because Ten was on the bench?)

680
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:12,400
(He literally threw the game.
Was he just there for fun?)

681
00:44:12,440 --> 00:44:13,840
(Get a new captain.)

682
00:44:35,880 --> 00:44:36,640
P'Three,

683
00:44:38,040 --> 00:44:40,400
can I ask you something?

684
00:44:44,200 --> 00:44:45,440
Is it about Ten and me?

685
00:44:47,400 --> 00:44:50,240
If you're not ready
to talk about it yet, it's okay.

686
00:44:51,520 --> 00:44:54,520
Whenever you're ready,
you can always talk to me.

687
00:45:13,200 --> 00:45:13,960
P'Three,

688
00:45:15,800 --> 00:45:17,160
can I ask you a favor?

689
00:45:21,080 --> 00:45:23,240
I want another plushie.

690
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:26,240
- Can you catch one for me?
- Huh?

691
00:45:27,920 --> 00:45:28,760
Right now?

692
00:45:29,440 --> 00:45:30,360
Yes. Let's go.

693
00:45:30,560 --> 00:45:32,560
Whoa, we're going now?

694
00:45:34,880 --> 00:45:35,560
P'Three,

695
00:45:36,080 --> 00:45:37,040
I want this one.

696
00:45:38,200 --> 00:45:39,800
Don't you already have that?

697
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:40,920
Why don't we get a different one?

698
00:45:41,440 --> 00:45:42,440
Please.

699
00:45:45,400 --> 00:45:46,960
Alright, fine.

700
00:45:46,960 --> 00:45:50,280
♪The answer is you
whenever I ask my heart♪

701
00:45:50,760 --> 00:45:51,920
What the hell?

702
00:45:53,760 --> 00:45:57,600
♪I'm afraid that
love could pull us apart♪

703
00:45:57,640 --> 00:46:00,680
♪If I'm the only one
who's loving with all my heart♪

704
00:46:00,800 --> 00:46:03,960
♪So many times I've rehearsed the line♪

705
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:06,520
Don't be so stressed.

706
00:46:08,200 --> 00:46:09,920
Games are supposed to be fun,
aren't they?

707
00:46:10,440 --> 00:46:11,640
If you lose, you just play again.

708
00:46:12,280 --> 00:46:14,880
You told me that, remember?

709
00:46:15,160 --> 00:46:16,880
Looks like my student
is teaching me now.

710
00:46:18,160 --> 00:46:19,640
I'm not stressed at all. Promise.

711
00:46:19,720 --> 00:46:22,080
No more stress.
I'll get this one for you, okay?

712
00:46:23,160 --> 00:46:24,320
Don't be stressed.

713
00:46:24,760 --> 00:46:26,760
Don't worry about it, Derpy Kid.

714
00:46:29,880 --> 00:46:30,680
- Whoa!
- Hey!

715
00:46:31,520 --> 00:46:32,680
Whoa, whoa!

716
00:46:33,320 --> 00:46:36,120
Whoa, I'm a pro.
It's as if this was planned.

717
00:46:36,160 --> 00:46:38,520
Look at that.
We're all surprised, aren't we?

718
00:46:38,520 --> 00:46:40,400
- Let's head home.
- Wait a second.

719
00:46:40,440 --> 00:46:41,520
Who said anything about going home?

720
00:46:42,840 --> 00:46:44,760
Hey, P'Three! Whoa!

721
00:46:44,800 --> 00:46:46,400
Run! Quick!

722
00:46:46,440 --> 00:46:48,680
Excuse me. You can't do this.

723
00:46:48,880 --> 00:46:49,880
P'Three!

724
00:46:51,960 --> 00:46:55,320
- P'Three!
- Please stop. You can't do this.

725
00:46:55,560 --> 00:46:56,440
P'Three!

726
00:46:56,760 --> 00:46:58,960
Hey, stop right there.

727
00:47:03,440 --> 00:47:04,440
Alright, Chef.

728
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:07,960
What's on the menu today, Chef Soh?

729
00:47:09,640 --> 00:47:10,800
Hello, viewers.

730
00:47:10,920 --> 00:47:14,120
Today, I'll be making my signature dish.

731
00:47:14,360 --> 00:47:15,600
And what dish is it?

732
00:47:18,920 --> 00:47:20,360
- Pepper-hottie.
- Whoa!

733
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:23,400
Stop it. That's enough.

734
00:47:24,120 --> 00:47:25,480
That's nice! Keep going.

735
00:47:25,600 --> 00:47:28,480
I've only got two things on the menu.

736
00:47:28,680 --> 00:47:29,760
What are they?

737
00:47:29,920 --> 00:47:31,840
Love and affection.

738
00:47:31,880 --> 00:47:33,520
Aw!

739
00:47:35,200 --> 00:47:36,440
You're the cutest.

740
00:47:39,120 --> 00:47:40,680
- Nom-nom, Soh. Oh...
- Ow!

741
00:47:44,120 --> 00:47:47,280
♪I'll find my way
into your heart one day,♪

742
00:47:47,320 --> 00:47:49,920
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

743
00:47:51,600 --> 00:47:52,920
Wow, this is amazing.

744
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:53,800
P'Three...

745
00:47:57,840 --> 00:48:00,920
♪For now,
I'll just keep things brotherly♪

746
00:48:01,040 --> 00:48:03,200
♪While caring for you secretly♪

747
00:48:03,240 --> 00:48:05,320
- P'Three!
- Do it again.

748
00:48:05,760 --> 00:48:07,680
- No!
- Come on, do it again.

749
00:48:10,440 --> 00:48:12,080
Stop it. Let's just eat.

750
00:48:12,120 --> 00:48:14,400
- There's something on my lips. Wipe it.
- Stop.

751
00:48:14,400 --> 00:48:15,120
Come on.

752
00:48:16,440 --> 00:48:17,720
Oh, that's a nice finish.

753
00:48:17,720 --> 00:48:19,720
- Whoa...
- Whoa, is this the number one Support?

754
00:48:19,880 --> 00:48:20,720
Definitely.

755
00:48:20,760 --> 00:48:21,840
Finish them!

756
00:48:26,080 --> 00:48:28,640
How long has it been since I've had
this much fun playing a game?

757
00:48:29,920 --> 00:48:30,880
Thanks, Soh.

758
00:48:32,120 --> 00:48:34,480
♪By doing this every single day♪

759
00:48:34,480 --> 00:48:36,480
♪Even if you never look my way♪

760
00:48:36,480 --> 00:48:38,760
♪(You never look my way)♪

761
00:48:38,960 --> 00:48:40,400
I'm done with the phone.

762
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:42,040
Why?

763
00:48:44,920 --> 00:48:46,680
There you go. That's perfect.

764
00:48:48,360 --> 00:48:49,080
P'Three...

765
00:48:50,360 --> 00:48:52,000
Can I ask you something?

766
00:48:52,480 --> 00:48:57,280
♪I'll get closer
until your heart belongs to me♪

767
00:49:03,160 --> 00:49:04,840
You want to know what happened
between me and Ten, right?

768
00:49:12,200 --> 00:49:13,720
Back then, the three of us...

769
00:49:14,720 --> 00:49:15,880
were best friends.

770
00:49:21,440 --> 00:49:25,000
We ate, stayed over,
and gamed together since high school.

771
00:49:27,240 --> 00:49:28,960
- (Nice. Let's go!)
- (Yeah!)

772
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:31,760
- (Help me out, Three.)
- (Seriously? You need my help?)

773
00:49:31,800 --> 00:49:33,320
- (Whoa, what the hell?)
- (Hey!)

774
00:49:33,320 --> 00:49:35,160
- (We're on the same team.)
- (I'm coming down.)

775
00:49:35,200 --> 00:49:36,840
(Alright, then. I'll finish them.)

776
00:49:37,080 --> 00:49:39,080
(Stick to the lane, bro.
Just like that!)

777
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:41,960
- (Go and be lame!)
- (Lane, not lame! Go!)

778
00:49:44,560 --> 00:49:45,520
(Nice!)

779
00:49:45,560 --> 00:49:47,000
- (Nice one.)
- (That's how it's done!)

780
00:49:47,040 --> 00:49:48,920
And that's how we formed Numb2r.

781
00:49:50,680 --> 00:49:51,160
(Jack! Ten!)

782
00:49:51,200 --> 00:49:52,600
- Because we had a dream...
- (Jack! Ten!)

783
00:49:52,640 --> 00:49:53,920
- (What?)
- (What is it?)

784
00:49:53,960 --> 00:49:55,320
- (I've got something to show you.)
- We dreamed that one day...

785
00:49:55,480 --> 00:49:56,480
(Take it! Here.)

786
00:49:56,560 --> 00:49:59,040
We'd stand on the stage together
as champions.

787
00:49:59,040 --> 00:50:00,920
- (Numb2r, baby!)
- (Number one!)

788
00:50:01,120 --> 00:50:02,120
(This is absolutely sick.)

789
00:50:02,160 --> 00:50:04,080
- (Isn't it too small?)
- (What do you mean?)

790
00:50:09,360 --> 00:50:12,400
But Ten ended up
misunderstanding everything.

791
00:50:14,960 --> 00:50:16,800
He thought Jack and I
didn't give a damn about him.

792
00:50:28,240 --> 00:50:30,720
- We did it!
- We're number one! Number one!

793
00:50:30,760 --> 00:50:34,040
(Congratulations on being named MVPs.)

794
00:50:34,520 --> 00:50:35,880
(Let me start with the first question.)

795
00:50:35,920 --> 00:50:37,520
(How are you feeling right now?)

796
00:50:38,280 --> 00:50:40,720
(Honestly, I'm super excited right now,)

797
00:50:40,760 --> 00:50:42,520
(and I'm really, really happy)

798
00:50:42,560 --> 00:50:45,160
(that everyone voted for us
to be the MVPs.)

799
00:50:45,520 --> 00:50:47,680
(Alright, thank you to all the fans)

800
00:50:47,680 --> 00:50:49,800
(who voted for us as MVPs today.)

801
00:50:49,800 --> 00:50:50,400
(Right.)

802
00:50:50,480 --> 00:50:52,200
(Alright, another question...)

803
00:50:53,120 --> 00:50:55,680
He felt like he wasn't
as important as Jack and me.

804
00:50:56,080 --> 00:50:57,480
But actually,

805
00:50:57,880 --> 00:50:59,440
we never felt that way about him at all.

806
00:51:01,360 --> 00:51:02,320
Damn it!

807
00:51:05,800 --> 00:51:06,880
Right before the finals,

808
00:51:08,160 --> 00:51:10,600
Ten sold our strategies
to the rival team...

809
00:51:15,800 --> 00:51:17,440
in exchange for a contract with them.

810
00:51:19,800 --> 00:51:22,000
- What the hell did you do?
- What's your f*cking problem?

811
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:24,360
- What the f*ck is wrong with you?
- That's enough!

812
00:51:24,480 --> 00:51:25,720
A loss is a loss.

813
00:51:25,800 --> 00:51:26,880
Stop blaming each other.

814
00:51:26,920 --> 00:51:28,200
How can I not blame him?

815
00:51:28,240 --> 00:51:30,040
He f*cking sold
our team's strategies to them!

816
00:51:30,200 --> 00:51:31,240
Stop it, Three!

817
00:51:34,240 --> 00:51:35,040
Ten.

818
00:51:36,160 --> 00:51:37,040
Just say it.

819
00:51:37,400 --> 00:51:39,160
Tell me you didn't do
something that sh*tty.

820
00:51:39,320 --> 00:51:40,360
Say it!

821
00:51:40,640 --> 00:51:42,280
- Just say it!
- I did!

822
00:51:42,480 --> 00:51:43,640
I did it.

823
00:51:44,200 --> 00:51:45,840
I told them the plan.

824
00:51:46,400 --> 00:51:47,560
What are you gonna do about it?

825
00:51:48,120 --> 00:51:49,160
What now?

826
00:51:51,280 --> 00:51:52,400
Do you know why?

827
00:51:54,240 --> 00:51:56,120
Because I don't want to play
with you guys anymore!

828
00:52:13,320 --> 00:52:14,560
Goddammit!

829
00:52:17,560 --> 00:52:19,880
After that,

830
00:52:20,200 --> 00:52:22,880
Jack and I cut him off

831
00:52:25,120 --> 00:52:26,360
and never spoke to him again.

832
00:52:34,880 --> 00:52:37,960
Thank you for telling me about this.

833
00:52:40,840 --> 00:52:42,000
I wanted to beat Ten.

834
00:52:43,000 --> 00:52:43,880
I thought...

835
00:52:44,760 --> 00:52:46,720
it would make up for all that anger,

836
00:52:47,920 --> 00:52:50,120
but it turned out that what I did...

837
00:52:53,200 --> 00:52:55,320
ended up hurting
my own team's feelings instead.

838
00:53:14,680 --> 00:53:17,960
Even if everyone is mad
at you right now,

839
00:53:19,960 --> 00:53:21,200
I'm certain...

840
00:53:21,960 --> 00:53:24,360
that they're ready
to listen and forgive you

841
00:53:26,160 --> 00:53:27,960
because they're on the same team as you.

842
00:53:52,080 --> 00:53:53,240
Same here.

843
00:53:54,200 --> 00:53:55,720
I'm on your team,

844
00:53:57,560 --> 00:53:59,320
and I'll always be by your side.

845
00:54:40,400 --> 00:54:41,800
If you're here to talk about Three,

846
00:54:42,360 --> 00:54:43,480
I'm not interested.

847
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:46,160
I want to talk about us.

848
00:55:10,880 --> 00:55:13,320
Go ahead. Blame me however you want.

849
00:55:14,800 --> 00:55:15,840
I'm not here to blame you.

850
00:55:16,960 --> 00:55:18,280
I just want to be sure of one thing.

851
00:55:18,680 --> 00:55:20,440
Did you ask for that scrim...

852
00:55:20,800 --> 00:55:22,640
just to mess with Three?

853
00:55:26,680 --> 00:55:28,360
I can see right through your playstyle.

854
00:55:30,080 --> 00:55:31,880
You weren't planning on beating him.

855
00:55:32,720 --> 00:55:34,600
You just wanted to tilt him

856
00:55:34,880 --> 00:55:36,120
by using Soh as a tool.

857
00:55:36,680 --> 00:55:37,600
Am I right?

858
00:55:42,320 --> 00:55:44,120
I thought you said
we were gonna talk about us.

859
00:55:48,040 --> 00:55:49,120
Until the tournament is over,

860
00:55:50,560 --> 00:55:51,840
I'm not seeing you again.

861
00:55:55,440 --> 00:55:56,280
You and I

862
00:55:57,200 --> 00:55:58,960
are going back to being strangers.

863
00:56:00,400 --> 00:56:02,440
Because if I keep being your friend,

864
00:56:03,960 --> 00:56:05,600
I'll never be able
to stop worrying about you.

865
00:56:09,200 --> 00:56:11,120
So you're saying
you actually care about me?

866
00:56:14,600 --> 00:56:15,840
What about after the tournament?

867
00:56:23,240 --> 00:56:24,200
After the tournament,

868
00:56:24,800 --> 00:56:25,640
I promise

869
00:56:26,560 --> 00:56:27,680
I'll come back to you.

870
00:56:30,040 --> 00:56:31,400
Just don't give me the silent treatment.

871
00:56:32,400 --> 00:56:33,960
I'll listen
to everything you have to say

872
00:56:35,560 --> 00:56:37,280
like a friend should have done
a long time ago.

873
00:56:51,840 --> 00:56:53,720
And who said I wanted to be
just your friend?

874
00:57:06,200 --> 00:57:10,720
(We are B.S. Brothers)

875
00:57:28,880 --> 00:57:29,480
Sorry.

876
00:57:34,360 --> 00:57:35,200
To whom?

877
00:57:36,720 --> 00:57:37,600
The chair?

878
00:57:43,400 --> 00:57:44,280
I'm sorry.

879
00:57:45,600 --> 00:57:47,360
It's my fault I talked sh*t to you.

880
00:57:48,440 --> 00:57:50,920
I got too tilted yesterday.
I'm sorry, man.

881
00:57:56,120 --> 00:57:56,920
Fine, I'm sorry.

882
00:58:00,440 --> 00:58:02,520
But if you pull that crap again,

883
00:58:02,800 --> 00:58:05,720
I'll tell P'Pech
to kick you out as Captain.

884
00:58:06,440 --> 00:58:07,160
Got it?

885
00:58:09,080 --> 00:58:11,560
Look, the fact that you apologized

886
00:58:12,440 --> 00:58:13,880
and said sorry to the team,

887
00:58:14,640 --> 00:58:15,680
that's enough, man.

888
00:58:18,960 --> 00:58:19,760
I know

889
00:58:19,960 --> 00:58:21,040
that you did that

890
00:58:21,600 --> 00:58:23,080
because you wanted to
lead us to victory.

891
00:58:23,520 --> 00:58:25,040
If you ask us if we want to win,

892
00:58:25,560 --> 00:58:26,320
we definitely do.

893
00:58:26,640 --> 00:58:27,320
Right?

894
00:58:28,720 --> 00:58:29,480
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

895
00:58:31,000 --> 00:58:32,120
But I couldn't stand it

896
00:58:32,360 --> 00:58:34,640
if we lost without even having fun.

897
00:58:40,080 --> 00:58:41,560
I know I've never said this,

898
00:58:42,040 --> 00:58:43,160
but believe it or not,

899
00:58:45,120 --> 00:58:46,960
every time I play with you

900
00:58:47,000 --> 00:58:48,040
and everyone on the team,

901
00:58:48,760 --> 00:58:49,920
it's so much fun.

902
00:58:51,120 --> 00:58:52,920
I never wanted to go anywhere else.

903
00:58:55,440 --> 00:58:57,120
You all made me realize

904
00:58:57,280 --> 00:59:00,240
that playing as a team
is way more fun than playing solo.

905
00:59:02,160 --> 00:59:04,120
Don't get me wrong, bro.

906
00:59:05,000 --> 00:59:07,640
Our team's track record is total trash.

907
00:59:08,840 --> 00:59:09,960
But the thing is...

908
00:59:10,200 --> 00:59:13,000
playing with you guys
is just so much fun.

909
00:59:13,040 --> 00:59:14,120
Otherwise, I'd have left ages ago.

910
00:59:15,080 --> 00:59:18,360
Honestly, I should've been
the first to go,

911
00:59:18,840 --> 00:59:21,000
but the reason I stayed as your coach

912
00:59:21,760 --> 00:59:24,720
was because I get to play with you,

913
00:59:24,960 --> 00:59:25,960
all of you.

914
00:59:26,760 --> 00:59:28,360
I really can't leave you guys behind.

915
00:59:30,360 --> 00:59:31,360
Whoa!

916
00:59:31,480 --> 00:59:32,840
You're making yourself sound all cool.

917
00:59:33,040 --> 00:59:34,560
You have to stay anyway, don't you?

918
00:59:34,600 --> 00:59:35,920
This is your cafe, after all.

919
00:59:36,440 --> 00:59:37,800
Get out of my cafe.

920
00:59:38,120 --> 00:59:39,720
Get out! Now!

921
00:59:43,880 --> 00:59:44,480
Three,

922
00:59:45,480 --> 00:59:46,520
do you remember

923
00:59:46,880 --> 00:59:48,520
why we became friends
in the first place

924
00:59:49,320 --> 00:59:50,520
and why we played games together?

925
00:59:52,680 --> 00:59:54,200
Yeah, I do.

926
00:59:54,520 --> 00:59:55,280
I won't forget.

927
01:00:15,360 --> 01:00:17,240
- B.S. Brothers!
- B.S. Brothers!

928
01:00:17,240 --> 01:00:22,320
- Talk your sh*t, take the championship!
- Talk your sh*t, take the championship!

929
01:00:45,360 --> 01:00:49,240
(We are B.S. Brothers)

930
01:00:49,880 --> 01:00:51,160
Top lane, damn it!

931
01:00:52,520 --> 01:00:53,880
Wow, good job.

932
01:00:53,880 --> 01:00:56,040
- What? Where are you flying to?
- Help me out! Help!

933
01:00:56,040 --> 01:00:58,000
Where are you even flying to?

934
01:00:58,000 --> 01:01:00,000
Get the Dark Slayer.
I want that. Where are you?

935
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:03,240
- You go first. You're closest.
- I already did! Where are you?

936
01:01:03,280 --> 01:01:05,880
- On my way, wait a sec.
- Look, I'm already in!

937
01:01:05,880 --> 01:01:10,520
♪Birthday but with me♪

938
01:01:10,520 --> 01:01:13,680
♪Why is it always happening to me?♪

939
01:01:13,920 --> 01:01:17,880
♪The more it happens, the more I see♪

940
01:01:18,120 --> 01:01:20,000
♪Yeah, it must be♪

941
01:01:23,160 --> 01:01:27,280
♪(Yeah, it must be)♪

942
01:01:27,320 --> 01:01:31,200
♪The more it happens, the more I see♪

943
01:01:31,560 --> 01:01:33,560
♪Yeah, it must be♪

944
01:01:36,400 --> 01:01:38,520
Yeah, that's how it's done!

945
01:01:38,680 --> 01:01:39,760
P'Jack, push the top lane.

946
01:01:39,800 --> 01:01:40,920
Nice!

947
01:01:41,040 --> 01:01:42,440
Laem, finish them off.

948
01:01:42,480 --> 01:01:44,280
- That was impressive, P'Laem!
- Whoa!

949
01:01:46,040 --> 01:01:47,200
Wait, they're trying to shut us down.

950
01:01:47,200 --> 01:01:49,280
- Can they? Whoa, they missed.
- They messed up. They missed.

951
01:01:49,320 --> 01:01:50,480
This isn't right.

952
01:01:50,640 --> 01:01:51,680
Get the tower!

953
01:01:51,800 --> 01:01:53,560
- We can end it.
- Let's end it right here.

954
01:01:53,680 --> 01:01:55,800
Man, I wanted a real match,
not a match with some noobs.

955
01:01:57,320 --> 01:01:58,160
Bring it on.

956
01:02:00,160 --> 01:02:00,800
Nice.

957
01:02:01,240 --> 01:02:02,240
One, two.

958
01:02:04,160 --> 01:02:04,960
Perfect.

959
01:02:05,000 --> 01:02:06,560
Perfect as the stars, right?

960
01:02:09,800 --> 01:02:11,600
Whoa, that was close.

961
01:02:13,680 --> 01:02:14,680
Hey, Soh.

962
01:02:14,840 --> 01:02:15,440
Yes?

963
01:02:17,680 --> 01:02:19,320
I haven't asked you this yet.

964
01:02:20,360 --> 01:02:22,040
When you saw me acting like that,

965
01:02:22,080 --> 01:02:24,640
were you disappointed in me at all?

966
01:02:26,440 --> 01:02:27,920
You mean when you got tilted?

967
01:02:30,920 --> 01:02:31,600
Well...

968
01:02:33,640 --> 01:02:34,720
A little bit.

969
01:02:35,520 --> 01:02:39,000
Especially when you were shouting.

970
01:02:40,640 --> 01:02:41,480
Really?

971
01:02:41,720 --> 01:02:42,760
Hey, Soh!

972
01:02:44,760 --> 01:02:46,480
- Wait!
- I'm just kidding.

973
01:02:46,520 --> 01:02:48,040
Hey, how could you do that to me?

974
01:02:48,080 --> 01:02:49,280
- How could you?
- Ow, P'Three!

975
01:02:49,760 --> 01:02:50,600
Come here.

976
01:02:50,600 --> 01:02:52,400
I said I was just kidding.

977
01:02:53,320 --> 01:02:56,480
(What was that smacking sound just now?)

978
01:02:56,560 --> 01:02:57,640
(Whatever you're doing...)

979
01:02:59,160 --> 01:03:00,400
Come here.

980
01:03:03,200 --> 01:03:04,760
Okay, the joke's over.

981
01:03:05,200 --> 01:03:06,560
Now, tell me the truth.

982
01:03:10,640 --> 01:03:11,960
Did I ever make it seem like...

983
01:03:12,320 --> 01:03:13,880
I was disappointed in you?

984
01:03:15,840 --> 01:03:17,080
I'm sorry.

985
01:03:18,000 --> 01:03:20,120
I didn't want you
to see that side of me.

986
01:03:21,160 --> 01:03:23,520
I think it was a good thing, though.

987
01:03:24,360 --> 01:03:25,040
Is it?

988
01:03:26,000 --> 01:03:26,760
It is.

989
01:03:27,680 --> 01:03:31,280
I don't want to know you
just for your sweet talk or funny side.

990
01:03:32,360 --> 01:03:34,160
I want to know every side of you,

991
01:03:35,240 --> 01:03:36,960
whether it's the good or the bad.

992
01:03:44,120 --> 01:03:45,160
But from now on,

993
01:03:45,960 --> 01:03:47,720
you aren't allowed
to be stubborn with me anymore.

994
01:03:49,240 --> 01:03:51,000
And if I'm a good boy,

995
01:03:51,760 --> 01:03:53,320
what will you give me?

996
01:03:57,040 --> 01:03:58,560
What do I get?

997
01:04:02,320 --> 01:04:05,560
♪I'll just get into your heart someday♪

998
01:04:05,760 --> 01:04:08,120
♪By doing this every single day♪

999
01:04:08,160 --> 01:04:10,160
♪Even if you never look my way♪

1000
01:04:10,200 --> 01:04:12,400
♪(You never look my way)♪

1001
01:04:12,440 --> 01:04:16,080
♪Before you know it,
you'll want me to stay♪

1002
01:04:19,200 --> 01:04:22,360
♪I'll find my way
into your heart one day,♪

1003
01:04:22,400 --> 01:04:25,000
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

1004
01:04:25,040 --> 01:04:26,960
♪Before you even look my way,♪

1005
01:04:26,960 --> 01:04:29,480
♪(Before you even look my way)♪

1006
01:04:29,480 --> 01:04:32,440
♪Before you realize I'm here to stay♪

1007
01:04:32,960 --> 01:04:36,120
♪For now,
I'll just keep things brotherly♪

1008
01:04:36,120 --> 01:04:38,520
♪While caring for you secretly♪

1009
01:04:38,560 --> 01:04:41,560
♪I'll leave no signs for you to see♪

1010
01:04:42,760 --> 01:04:48,600
♪Until your heart makes room for me♪

1011
01:05:14,880 --> 01:05:16,000
Hey, AI buddy.

1012
01:05:18,320 --> 01:05:19,720
Help me.

1013
01:05:20,520 --> 01:05:26,120
My boyfriend
is really stressed out right now.

1014
01:05:28,040 --> 01:05:30,400
(Why don't you try
telling your boyfriend a joke?)

1015
01:05:30,400 --> 01:05:32,440
(Research shows that jokes and laughter)

1016
01:05:32,480 --> 01:05:35,440
(can significantly
reduce stress hormone levels.)

1017
01:05:35,520 --> 01:05:38,240
(Especially pickup lines about love)

1018
01:05:38,280 --> 01:05:40,880
(will help boost
positive feelings even better.)

1019
01:05:44,120 --> 01:05:52,520
But I don't know any jokes.

1020
01:05:53,000 --> 01:06:00,280
Can you list some good ones for me?

1021
01:06:02,360 --> 01:06:04,040
(Coming right up. Here is a list...)

1022
01:06:04,600 --> 01:06:08,280
(of the most popular cheesy lines
for an esports pro boyfriend.)

1023
01:06:13,640 --> 01:06:14,640
P'Three,

1024
01:06:15,160 --> 01:06:18,920
you're playing games so much.
Want to go for a run with me?

1025
01:06:20,040 --> 01:06:21,760
(What kind of run, Soh?)

1026
01:06:22,720 --> 01:06:27,400
Well, running through my mind
so that I'll love you all day.

1027
01:06:28,080 --> 01:06:29,000
(Oh, that's impressive.)

1028
01:06:29,040 --> 01:06:31,480
(I must say, your joke
and the way you delivered it)

1029
01:06:31,520 --> 01:06:33,480
(were very funny and romantic.)

1030
01:06:33,920 --> 01:06:36,960
(I'm sure your boyfriend
will definitely feel much better.)

1031
01:06:41,520 --> 01:06:43,080
♪Telling myself, "You'll be fine,"♪

1032
01:06:43,200 --> 01:06:45,680
♪'Cause trouble finds me every time♪

1033
01:06:45,920 --> 01:06:48,160
♪By PROXIE♪

1034
01:06:48,480 --> 01:06:51,240
♪I never wanted trouble in my way,♪

1035
01:06:52,400 --> 01:06:55,760
♪Yet somehow it keeps finding me always♪

1036
01:06:55,840 --> 01:06:57,600
♪I'm just out here doing my thing,♪

1037
01:06:57,640 --> 01:06:59,720
♪Goofing around, worrying 'bout nothing,♪

1038
01:06:59,760 --> 01:07:01,440
♪Then luck's gone cold, and love brought pain,♪

1039
01:07:01,480 --> 01:07:03,280
♪I've learned my lesson, no more love again♪

1040
01:07:03,280 --> 01:07:05,240
♪Yeah, I know, I said that last time, too♪

1041
01:07:05,280 --> 01:07:07,120
♪My friends went, "We've heard that from you"♪

1042
01:07:07,160 --> 01:07:08,960
♪Even my mom said, "Here we go, déjà vu"♪

1043
01:07:09,000 --> 01:07:11,600
♪Love keeps chasing me though I never ask it to♪

1044
01:07:12,160 --> 01:07:15,400
♪I don't know why fate keeps testing me♪

1045
01:07:15,480 --> 01:07:18,160
♪It's as if this was meant to be♪

1046
01:07:19,440 --> 01:07:23,040
♪A thousand thoughts keep running through,♪

1047
01:07:23,120 --> 01:07:24,760
♪But all I ever think about is you♪

1048
01:07:24,800 --> 01:07:29,480
♪Birthday but with me♪

1049
01:07:29,520 --> 01:07:32,880
♪Every time, it's just me and me only♪

1050
01:07:32,880 --> 01:07:36,520
♪What's this feeling? I've got no clue,♪

1051
01:07:36,640 --> 01:07:38,840
♪Could it be I'm missing you?♪

1052
01:07:39,920 --> 01:07:44,760
♪Birthday but with me♪

1053
01:07:44,800 --> 01:07:47,880
♪Why is it always happening to me?♪

1054
01:07:48,120 --> 01:07:51,640
♪The more it happens, the more I see♪

1055
01:07:52,280 --> 01:07:54,520
♪Yeah, it must be♪

1056
